# Repo docs must not be served. Netlify publishes the repo root (there is no
# netlify.toml), so a markdown file at the root is served like any other asset:
# /CLAUDE.md returned HTTP 200 on the live site until this rule. The ! is
# required for the same reason as the host rules below: the file exists, and an
# unforced rule is ignored in favour of serving it (verified on deploy preview 5).
# Dotfiles (.claude/*, .gitignore) are already refused by Netlify and need no rule.
/CLAUDE.md                       /404.html                                                              404!

# Old paths — absolute targets so either host reaches the canonical page in one hop
/slides/*                        https://boulderbiologics.net/how-it-works.html                     301
/how-to-add-orthobiologics.html  https://boulderbiologics.net/how-to-add-autologous-biologics.html  301

# Retired domain — everything left goes to the canonical host, path preserved.
# The ! is required: the page files all exist, and without it Netlify serves the file instead of redirecting.
http://orthobiopartners.com/*    https://boulderbiologics.net/:splat   301!
https://orthobiopartners.com/*   https://boulderbiologics.net/:splat   301!
